1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:12,136
Close your eyes for a second. Now try to use Instagram. Every photo just says, image. Every feed is endless swiping. This is The Coop. Social media you can hear.

2
00:00:13,336 --> 00:00:22,432
On The Coop, the post is the sound. Friends share audio journeys, where they went and how it felt, in their own voices. Here's Maya.

3
00:00:22,932 --> 00:00:42,956
Maya: Ocean Beach, six in the morning. The sand is cold and packed hard, and the waves come in sets of three: boom, hiss, quiet. My cane found a line of seaweed and I followed it to the water. Salt on my lips, wind pushing my hood back. Honestly, it felt like the whole ocean was saying good morning.

4
00:00:43,956 --> 00:00:56,172
You don't swipe. You talk. Say next, like it, or reply, and Coo, our friendly pigeon, takes care of it. You can interrupt any time.

5
00:00:57,372 --> 00:01:04,476
If a friend shares a photo, ask Coo to describe it, then ask anything about it. Coo never guesses who someone is.

6
00:01:05,676 --> 00:01:13,524
The news is real, from the last two days, with a focus on good news for the blind community. Coo always says where it came from.

7
00:01:14,724 --> 00:01:22,332
Ask how to get a ride in San Jose, and Coo searches only official sites, like the city's paratransit service.

8
00:01:23,532 --> 00:01:28,740
And learn new skills, like cooking without sight, explained in three simple steps.

9
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:38,196
In support circles, scams are held before anyone hears them, and Coo asks, are you sure, before anything risky.

10
00:01:39,396 --> 00:01:47,364
Websites that don't work with a screen reader? Just say, do it for me. Manus does the clicking, and always stops for your yes.

11
00:01:48,564 --> 00:01:57,060
Coo can even call Grandma's landline to share a journey, and turn posts into captioned clips, so sighted friends can join in.

12
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:03,324
Built for blind people first. Better for everyone. Scan the code to try The Coop.
